{{also|erde}}
==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|goh|erda}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*erþō}}. Compare {{cog|nl|aarde}}, {{cog|fy|ierde}}, {{cog|en|earth}}, {{cog|da|jord}}, {{cog|got|𐌰𐌹𐍂𐌸𐌰}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈeːɐ̯də/|[ˈʔeːɐ̯də]|lang=de}} {{i|standard}}
* {{IPA|/ˈɛʁdə/|[ˈʔɛʁdə]|[ˈʔɛɐ̯də]|lang=de}} {{i|by a common merger}}
* {{audio|de-Erde.ogg|audio|lang=de}}
* {{rhymes|eːɐ̯də|lang=de}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|f|Erde|Erden}}

# {{lb|de|uncountable}} [[soil]]
#: {{ux|de|Sie nahm eine Handvoll '''Erde'''.|t=She took a handful of '''soil.'''|inline=1}}
# {{lb|de|uncountable}} the [[ground]]
#: {{ux|de|Er fiel auf die '''Erde'''.|t=He fell on the '''ground.'''|inline=1}}
# {{lb|de|countable}} a [[world]]; a space to live in
#: {{ux|de|Diese '''Erde''' wird vergehen, aber Gott wird eine neue '''Erde''' schaffen.|t=This '''earth''' will fade, but God will create a new '''earth.'''}}

